  "title": "The Easy Question Half of Harvard Got Wrong #shorts",
  "description": "A bat and a ball cost $1.10. The bat costs $1 more than the ball. Maya says 10 cents instantly; it's 5 cents. In Shane Frederick's Cognitive Reflection Test (Journal of Economic Perspectives, 2005), about half of students at Harvard, MIT and Princeton gave the intuitive wrong answer. The fast answer feels right, so we don't check it. #psychology #shorts #riddle #brainteaser",
